  "badger": "frames are 16 px high but wider than a tile (17-18 px front/back, 26 px from the side). Centre them on the tile: x = tileX*16 + 8 - w/2, y = tileY*16 - 1",
  "shadow": "draw badger_shadow_side (moving left/right) or badger_shadow_front (up/down) at the tile position, under the badger",
  "facing": "idle frame = the direction it last moved; the old file names badger_front_idle / badger_back_idle are badger_down_idle / badger_up_idle here",
  "dug_ground": "a dug tile is dug_0 when (x + y) is odd, dug_1 when even. On top of it add dug_edge_top / _left / _bottom / _right for every side whose neighbour is NOT dug (sunken shade at the top and left, heaped crumbs at the bottom and right)",
  "warning": "before a tile is dug, overlay warn_cracks on the next 3 tiles of the badger's path: warn_cracks_2 on the very next tile, _1 on the one after, _0 on the third",
  "clods": "client-only dirt spray: each frame the badger moves, drop about 5 clods 8-16 px behind it (random spread a few px), alternating clod_0 / clod_1; they can fade after ~10 ticks"
